---
// Roof cleaning — a LEAF page under the Home Cleaning mega-menu's third
// group, "Outside your home" (navigation.ts). Built in the same pass as
// window, gutter, high pressure and exterior house washing.
//
// Its middle is a `ContentGrid` of image/text pairs rather than the window
// page's persona cards or the gutter page's day-in-the-life story, because
// this page has to teach one thing before it can sell anything: the black on
// a roof is alive, and blasting it is how roofs get wrecked. That argument
// needs a picture beside each paragraph.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS for any of the five. All copy below is DRAFTED, not
// supplied, and needs sign-off. Facts only TLB holds ship as [brackets].
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - WORKING AT HEIGHT, and here it is worse than the gutter page: this is
//     time spent ON the roof surface, not at the edge of it. Confirm training,
//     harness and anchor practice, and that insurance covers it, before this
//     publishes.
//   - IS THIS DELIVERED IN HOUSE? Soft washing needs a low pressure unit and
//     the right chemistry. If it is subcontracted, §8's comparison table
//     ("employed by TLB, not subcontracted") contradicts the page and comes
//     off it.
//   - WHAT SOLUTION DO WE USE, AND WHAT DOES IT DO TO THE GARDEN? §3 and
//     branded FAQ 4 both promise plants are wet down and protected.
//     Sodium hypochlorite based mixes are the industry norm and they will
//     kill plants if run off untreated. Confirm the product, the dilution and
//     the garden protocol. This is the biggest complaint risk on the page.
//   - TILE, COLORBOND, OR BOTH? §5 treats them differently and it should.
//     Confirm TLB does both, and confirm whether anything is declined
//     (asbestos cement sheeting is the one that matters, see below).
//   - ⚠️ ASBESTOS. Older fibre cement roofing and eave sheeting can contain
//     asbestos, and cleaning it disturbs the surface. Non-branded FAQ 4 says
//     we do not touch it. Confirm that is the policy, because it must be.
//   - PAINTING AND RESTORATION. We are cleaning, not recoating. Branded FAQ 5
//     says so. Confirm TLB does not want to offer restoration, or that answer
//     changes.
//   - PRICING BASIS and minimum charge. Bracketed in non-branded FAQ 5.
//   - [insured] in §6 is inherited from the commercial hub.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: four generated assets of its own in
// src/assets/home_cleaning/outside_your_home/roof_cleaning/, prompts in the
// IMAGE-PROMPTS.md beside them, plus the cluster's shared backdrop one level
// up. Uniform deviation as per the group, plus a harness on the two roof
// frames, which is the point of them.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import ContentGrid from '../../components/sections/ContentGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/sections/BeforeAfter.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
// Shared across all five pages in this group. See the window page's note.
// SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See §7.
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, comparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { locationGroups } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherOutsideServices } from '../../data/outsideYourHome';
import { theLineHeading, howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

// §0 Metadata. "Roof cleaning" leads. "Soft washing" is the method and is
// carried in body copy, because almost nobody searches for it and everybody
// searches for the problem.
//
// Title and description are the SIGNED-OFF workbook text (Keyword Mapping &
// Metadata, sheet 1 row 15), reproduced verbatim. The old title was the
// shortest of the eight and left 22 characters unused, dropping
// `roof cleaning services` (300/mo) and `cleaning roof tiles` (150/mo); the
// old description ran 33 characters over, so "without high pressure" — the
// page's entire differentiator — was being truncated out of the result.
//
// 🔴 BLOCKS LAUNCH. The approved description states "Fully insured" as a plain
// fact. BFD 2.4 has insurance unconfirmed and says directly: "Police checked
// and insured appears in supplied meta descriptions. Confirm both before
// publishing." §3's third explainer block still renders the literal [insured]
// placeholder. On a job that means walking on somebody's roof, this is the
// claim they rely on most. Same finding as the gutter page; one decision
// resolves both.
//
// ⚠️ ALSO WORTH A SECOND LOOK: "without damage". The page argues that case
// properly across §3, §4 and §5, so it is defensible as a description of what
// soft washing does rather than a promise about outcome — but BFD 12.2 rules
// out guarantees of any kind and this is one adjective away from reading as
// one. Suggested replacement once insurance is confirmed, from
// roof-cleaning-copy-rewrite.md, at 131 characters:
//   'Roof cleaning that clears moss, lichen and years of grime from roof tiles
//    and metal roofs, by soft washing. Get a free quote today.'
//
// In `pageMeta`, on `canonical`:
// ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.

// The page's one primary CTA, per BFD 9.5, repeated on every in-page button.
// `Get a free quote today` is the approved workbook CTA and it fits a button
// at 22 characters, so it goes on unchanged.
//
// It also resolves a BFD 13.2 conflict: the old `Get an instant quote`
// promised instant pricing on a page whose own pricing block says the honest
// answer is a fast quote, and whose last FAQ says the rate moves with pitch,
// access, roof type and how heavy the growth is. A free quote is a different
// promise from an instant price and it is one this page can keep. "Free" is
// not on the BFD banned pricing list, which covers cheap, budget, affordable,
// competitive rates and premium, so the approved wording is compliant.
//
// The header keeps the site-wide quoteCta — that is chrome, not this page.

// §1 Hero. The H1 now carries the mapped primary `roof cleaning` (1,600/mo) as
// an exact contiguous phrase, extended with the region because
// `roof cleaning near me` (500/mo) and `roof pressure cleaning near me`
// (150/mo) sit behind the term. The old heading — the sentence people actually
// say to each other when they pull into the driveway — is not cut: it opens
// the lead, which is the only place it survives, because its whole effect
// comes from withholding the subject until the second clause.
//
// The subheading is a NEW line. Its extension is method and material rather
// than the H1's region, and it puts soft washing and low pressure above the
// fold, which is the decision this page exists to influence. Branded FAQ 3
// confirms colorbond belongs in the promise.
//
// Scene photo, family A, square source so the 1/1 box crops nothing. The
// harness is deliberately visible.

// §2 Definition. The answer target. Paragraph two does the work almost no
// competitor page in this category does honestly: it separates the method from
// the service, and it says out loud that the cheap version of this job causes
// damage.

// §3 The teaching block. `ContentGrid` at two columns, laid out purely by
// array order the way `StoryMosaic` is, so image and text swap sides by
// position alone. `StoryMosaic` itself cannot be used here: its `image` block
// has no `src` field, so it can only ever render a placeholder, and this page
// has real photos. Flagged in SECTIONS.md's own note about the deliberate
// overlap between the two.
//
// Three rows: what the black is, what a soft wash does, who arrives. The
// third row exists because the two above it are technical, and the reader
// still has to let a stranger onto their roof.
//
// In `explainerBlocks`, on the first paragraph of "Who is on your roof":
// ⚠️ [insured] inherited from the commercial hub. One answer fixes every
// page.

// §4 The warning. `Callout` `warning` tone, used once. This is the single most
// useful paragraph on the page for a reader about to accept the cheapest
// quote, and it makes no claim about TLB at all.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFY THE WORDING. Manufacturer guidance for concrete roof tiles and
// prepainted steel roofing both advise against high pressure cleaning, and
// stripping a tile's surface coating is the well established failure mode.
// Stated here as behaviour rather than as legal or warranty advice, with no
// pressure figure and no brand named. If TLB wants a source on the page, the
// tile and steel manufacturers' own care guidance is the honest one.

// §5 Scope of work. `ServiceBlocks` icon grid. Six stages in the order they
// happen, and the last two are the ones a homeowner never thinks to ask about
// and always cares about afterwards.
//
// ⚠️ EVERY ITEM IS DRAFTED against ordinary practice, not supplied by TLB.
// Confirm each and cut what TLB does not do. Two carry blockers, marked.
//
// In `scopeItems`, on "Solution on, and time to work":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm the product and dilution. See the file header.
// In `scopeItems`, on "Plants and pets protected":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER, and the biggest complaint risk on the page.

// §6 Timing. Short dark block. The one genuinely useful piece of local advice
// on the page, and it doubles as the reason not to wait.

// §7 Before and after. SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See the window
// page's §6 note, which applies verbatim.
//
// THE PHOTO BRIEF for a real pair: one roof plane, shot from a fixed position
// (a ladder at the ridge, or the same upstairs window both times), before and
// after, nothing moved between frames. A tiled roof with heavy streaking is
// the most persuasive subject in this entire category, and it is worth the
// tripod.

// §8 The rest of the cluster. Shared data, this page's own href filtered out.
const siblingItems = otherOutsideServices('/house-cleaning/roof-cleaning/');

// §9 Comparison table. Shared rows from src/data/comparison.ts.
//
// ⚠️ CONDITIONAL. Row one is "employed by TLB, not subcontracted". If roof
// work is subcontracted, the table contradicts the page and comes off it.

// §11 Branded FAQs, in the customer's voice. Self-contained 40 to 80 word
// answers, per BFD 3.5.
//
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Do you do colorbond as well as tiles?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm both are done. See the file header.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "What about our garden and our pets?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. See §5.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Can you paint or restore the roof too?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm TLB does not want to offer this.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED:
//   - Algae, moss and lichen being living growth rather than dirt, and lichen
//     anchoring into the tile surface, are both standard and correct.
//   - High pressure stripping the surface coating of concrete tiles is the
//     established failure mode and matches manufacturer care guidance.
//   - ⚠️ ASBESTOS. The answer below states we do not clean fibre cement
//     roofing that may contain asbestos. This must match TLB's actual policy
//     before publishing, and it is worded as a referral rather than as advice.
//   - Frequency is hedged as an observation with shade as the variable.
//   - Pricing bracketed on purpose.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "Can old fibre cement roofing be cleaned?":
// ⚠️ MUST MATCH TLB'S ACTUAL POLICY. See the note above this array.
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "How much does roof cleaning cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE.

// §13 Closing CTA.

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/roof-cleaning.yaml and is
// edited in Pages CMS ("Roof cleaning"). This file owns the layout. The notes
// above explain why each section says what it says; they stay here because
// Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/roof-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    // The text of the page's one primary button. It always links to the
    // site-wide quote page, so only the words are editable.
    buttonLabel: section.text,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    explainer: section.contentGrid,
    warning: section.callout,
    method: section.iconGrid,
    beforeAfter: section.beforeAfter,
    timing: section.textBlock,
    // The rows are the shared outside-your-home cross-links.
    otherServices: section.sectionIntro,
    // The columns and rows are the shared comparison table (Site settings).
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud,
    bookingFaq: section.faq,
    generalFaq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/roof-cleaning/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW, the Tweed and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const pageCta = { ...quoteCta, label: page.buttonLabel };

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

// Photo cells are laid out at 4:3.
const explainerBlocks = page.explainer.items.map((item) =>
  item.type === 'image' ? { type: 'image' as const, ...sized(item.image, '4/3') } : item,
);

---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? pageCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90} focus="bottom">
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    {/* Two columns, and which side each block lands on is purely its position
        in the array. Row one is image then text, row two text then image, row
        three image then text. */}
    <ContentGrid
      heading={page.explainer.heading}
      lead={page.explainer.lead}
      columns={2}
      blocks={explainerBlocks}
    />

    <Callout tone="warning" heading={page.warning.heading} body={page.warning.body} cta={page.warning.cta} />

    {/* 🔑 The keyword H2. Third exact instance of `roof cleaning`, after the
        H1 and the hero subheading, and the ceiling — the second FAQ heading
        below gives the phrase up rather than becoming a fourth. Its extension
        is process, and "stage by stage" describes the six items beneath it. */}
    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.method.heading}
      lead={page.method.lead}
      items={page.method.items}
      cta={page.method.cta ?? pageCta}
    />

    <BeforeAfter
      heading={page.beforeAfter.heading}
      lead={page.beforeAfter.lead}
      pairs={page.beforeAfter.pairs}
      note={page.beforeAfter.note}
      beforeLabel={page.beforeAfter.beforeLabel}
      afterLabel={page.beforeAfter.afterLabel}
    />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.timing.heading}
      body={page.timing.body}
      cta={page.timing.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.timing.backgroundImage}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherServices.heading}
      lead={page.otherServices.lead}
      items={siblingItems}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={comparisonRows}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={theLineHeading.fast}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* Both FAQ headings renamed. The first five questions are about whether
        it comes back, walking on tiles, colorbond, gardens and pets, and
        whether TLB also paints — all pre-booking questions, and this matches
        the carpet page's "Booking a carpet clean". "Roof clean" rather than
        "roof cleaning" is deliberate: three exact instances is the ceiling and
        they are spent. The second heading carried the phrase as a fourth, so
        it gives it up; its replacement describes the block accurately and
        picks up `cleaning roof tiles` (150/mo), which the old one did not. */}
    <Faq heading={page.bookingFaq.heading} lead={page.bookingFaq.lead} items={page.bookingFaq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.generalFaq.heading} lead={page.generalFaq.lead} items={page.generalFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? pageCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
